# Example configuration. Contains no secrets.
#
# The real environment URL is deliberately NOT committed: it identifies a tenant.
# Pass it on the command line instead, so the destination of every deploy is
# explicit and auditable:
#
#   npm run start  -- --environment-url https://YOUR-ENVIRONMENT-ID.apps.dynatrace.com/
#   npm run deploy -- --environment-url https://YOUR-ENVIRONMENT-ID.apps.dynatrace.com/ \
#                     --optimize --enable-code-splitting
#
# This app needs no API token and no client secret. Authentication is handled by
# AppEngine at runtime and by the dt-app CLI session at deploy time. If you find
# yourself wanting to put a credential here, something has gone wrong.

DT_ENVIRONMENT_URL=https://YOUR-ENVIRONMENT-ID.apps.dynatrace.com/
